            <div xml:id="d496">

                <pb facs="1053" n="1013" xml:id="pg1013"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">674.84A/9–2752: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 496<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Israel (Davis) to the
                        Department of State</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d496-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Tel
                                Aviv</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1952-09-27T19:00:00+03:00">September 27, 1952—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>498. Re Embtel 422.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d496-f2"/> VD chief Amer Div Fon
                    Ministry advises informal mtg with Egypt MAC rep Gohar took place Thursday
                    September 25 with Col Ramati representing IG pursuant to arrangement described
                    in ref tel. IG rep made specific suggestion that special mtg be arranged on
                    higher level to discuss (1) broadening scope of present anti-infiltration
                    agreement and (2) resolving questions of mutual interest relating to shipping.
                    Egypt’s rep said he wld consult superiors and report result. IG hopes discussion
                    of point (1) may lead to gen non-aggression agreement; and as to point (2) it
                    proposes cover all shipping matters including territorial waters, fishing rights
                    and possibly passage of shipping through Suez Canal (see Embtels 467 and
                        497).<anchor n="3" xml:id="d496-f3"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
